KZ2 patch 2184: a shader's Metal compile runs outside the translator lock.

Written for the Pyrrhus native Mac bring-up; no game code or RPCS3 code used.
Licence: MIT (project LICENSE).

eng_function held s_eng_translate_lock (patch 2179: the HLSL->MSL translator
and its scratch buffers are not reentrant) across compile_guest_function too,
i.e. across newLibraryWithSource, tens of milliseconds a shader. The four build
workers -- with the 256 pipelines the boot prewarm of patch 2181 queues -- took
turns on that lock for whole compiles, and the FIFO walker, when it needed a
pipeline at once (the 2179 retry of an entry older than 5 s), queued behind
them on a mutex that is not fair. A wall-clock sample of the walker in gameplay
(RSX_WALKER_PROF) had 41.9 % of its time in __psynch_mutexwait under
eng_function; the log showed drains of 1-3 s with no build "waited for".

The translation stays under the lock; the compile runs on a private copy of the
MSL text after it is released. Two builders that compile the same text at once
keep the first entry (a duplicate compile, never a lost or wrong function).

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m b/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
index 3ffb64b..cb4b887 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_metal_backend.m
@@ -3592,7 +3592,24 @@ static u32 eng_depth_as_color(void* user, u32 depth, u32 w, u32 h, u32 rsx_fmt)
         snprintf(name, sizeof name, "%s_%016llx.msl", what, (unsigned long long)hash);
         dump_shader(name, s_msl);
         snprintf(name, sizeof name, "%s %016llx", what, (unsigned long long)hash);
-        fn = compile_guest_function(s_msl, name);
+        /* KZ2 patch 2184: only the translator and its scratch buffers need the lock. The Metal compile
+         * (tens of ms) ran under it too, so the four build workers -- 256 of them queued by the boot prewarm --
+         * took turns on it for the whole compile, and a walker that needed one pipeline now (the 2179 retry)
+         * waited behind them on a mutex that is not fair: 42 % of the walker's wall time in a gameplay
+         * sample, drains of 1-3 s. The compile now runs on a private copy of the text, outside the lock. */
+        char* const msl = strdup(s_msl);
+        pthread_mutex_unlock(&s_eng_translate_lock);
+        if (msl) { fn = compile_guest_function(msl, name); free(msl); }
+        pthread_mutex_lock(&s_eng_translate_lock);
+        /* Another builder may have compiled the same text meanwhile: keep the first entry. */
+        for (u32 i = 0; i < s_eng_func_count; i++)
+            if (s_eng_func[i].hash == hash) {
+                const id<MTLFunction> hit = s_eng_func[i].fn ? s_eng_func[i].fn : fn;
+                s_eng_func[i].fn = hit;
+                pthread_mutex_unlock(&s_eng_translate_lock);
+                return hit;
+            }
+        if (s_eng_func_count >= ENG_MAX_FUNCS) { pthread_mutex_unlock(&s_eng_translate_lock); return fn; }
     }
     s_eng_func[s_eng_func_count].hash = hash;
     s_eng_func[s_eng_func_count].fn   = fn;
